":"(node:83740) ExperimentalWarning: localStorage is not available because --localstorage-file was not provided.\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\n/var/folders/j4/4j7qn2vd4zd6ykklypxn1d540000gn/T/perigee-results.9Xj5K0Y1zD/tmp/template-inspect/template-manifest.json\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":10,"nanos":586063459},"formatted_output":"(node:83740) ExperimentalWarning: localStorage is not available because --localstorage-file was not provided.\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\n/var/folders/j4/4j7qn2vd4zd6ykklypxn1d540000gn/T/perigee-results.9Xj5K0Y1zD/tmp/template-inspect/template-manifest.json\n"},"started_at_ms":1789292181248,"completed_at_ms":1789292191835}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:27.963Z","ordinal":4450,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0612ff0593abfece016aa66e9c2be887d2bd6f454ee7c6370c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2tzweIkkqEa8DSmNLNTLV2GH","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: web/src/lib/pitch-content.ts\\n@@\\n-  modelStatus: 'Retraining pending',\\n+  model: { name: 'OpenTSLM · balanced sampling', detail: 'LoRA · retrained on the event-grouped split', accuracy: '75.89%', precision: '0.837', recall: '0.643', f1: '0.727' },\\n+  confusion: { trueNegative: 98, falsePositive: 14, falseNegative: 40, truePositive: 72 },\\n+  categories: { rareEvent: { detected: 49, total: 74 }, anomaly: { detected: 23, total: 38 } },\\n*** Update File: web/src/components/evidence.tsx\\n@@\\n-      <article><strong>—</strong><span>OpenTSLM · retraining pending</span></article>\\n+      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.model.accuracy}</strong><span>OpenTSLM · accuracy</span></article>\\n@@\\n-    <p className=\\\"landing-result-note\\\">The evaluation now keeps each event in one split. Baselines rerun; OpenTSLM retraining pending. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\\n+    <p className=\\\"landing-result-note\\\">OpenTSLM outperforms the two-shot LLM baseline. Classical summary statistics still lead at 90.18%. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\\n@@\\n-          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. Its 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 are the comparison target for the retrained OpenTSLM system. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\\n-          <p>All previous fine-tuned scores were measured on the old split with cross-channel event leakage. A corrected-split OpenTSLM result is not yet available. We do not compare those old model scores against the new baselines.</p>\\n+          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. It leads with 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 versus OpenTSLM at 75.89% and 0.727. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\\n+          <p>OpenTSLM SP with sub-category-balanced sampling was retrained on the corrected split using an H200. It correctly classifies 170 of 224 windows: 98 nominal and 72 positive, with 14 false positives and 40 missed positive windows. Precision is 0.837, recall 0.643 and F1 0.727. Rare Event recall is 66.2% (49/74); Anomaly recall is 60.5% (23/38). These replace the old-split headline scores. Checkpoint selection used validation loss; the selected checkpoint was epoch 7.</p>\\n*** Update File: web/public/mission-control/README.md\\n@@\\n-The pitch checklist requires retraining OpenTSLM on the corrected split. Results do not establish\\n+The pitch checklist now reports a retrained OpenTSLM result of 75.89% accuracy and\\n+F1 0.727 on the corrected split; that separate run is not this replay. Results do not establish\\n*** End Patch\"));\nconst changes=[\n['web/src/components/evidence.tsx','pitchBenchmark.results.map(result','[pitchBenchmark.model, ...pitchBenchmark.results].map(result'],\n['web/tests/experience.spec.ts',\"await expect(evidence).toContainText('OpenTSLM retraining pending');\",\"await expect(evidence).toContainText('75.89%');\\n  await expect(evidence).not.toContainText('retraining pending');\"],\n['web/tests/experience.spec.ts',\"[['Two-shot Llama-3.2-3B', '50.45%']\",\"[['OpenTSLM · balanced sampling', '75.89%'], ['Two-shot Llama-3.2-3B', '50.45%']\"],\n['web/README.md','All fine-tuned OpenTSLM scores need reproducing on the corrected split; the site shows retraining pending, not an old score against new baselines.','OpenTSLM SP with sub-category-balanced sampling has now been retrained on the corrected split using an H200: 75.89% accuracy (170/224), P 0.837, R 0.643, F1 0.727. Confusion counts: TN 98, FP 14, FN 40, TP 72. Rare Event recall is 66.2% (49/74); Anomaly recall is 60.5% (23/38). It outperforms the two-shot LLM but remains behind the restricted classical baseline. The selected checkpoint was epoch 7, chosen by validation loss (0.4377).']\n];\nfor(const[path,old,next]of changes){\nconst source=(await tools.exec_command({cmd:`cat ${path}`,max_output_tokens:15000})).output;\nconst line=source.split('\\n').find(l=>l.includes(old));if(!line)throw Error(path);\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(`*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: ${path}\\n@@\\n-${line}\\n+${line.replace(old,next).split('\\n').join('\\n+')}\\n*** End Patch`));\n}\nconst root=(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat Docs/PITCH_REQUIREMENTS_CHECKLIST.md\",max_output_tokens:14000})).output;\nconst old=(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat web/Docs/PITCH_REQUIREMENTS_CHECKLIST.md\",max_output_tokens:14000})).output;\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(`*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: web/Docs/PITCH_REQUIREMENTS_CHECKLIST.md\\n@@\\n-${old.trimEnd().split('\\n').join('\\n-')}\\n+${root.trimEnd().split('\\n').join('\\n+')}\\n*** End Patch`));\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: web/tests/unit/pitch-content.test.ts\\n@@\\n-    expect(pitchBenchmark.modelStatus).toBe('Retraining pending');\\n     expect(pitchBenchmark.results.every(result => !result.name.includes('OpenTSLM'))).toBe(true);\\n   });\\n+  it('checks the retrained model against the new table and confusion counts', () => {\\n+    const section = checklist.split('| Metric | Leaky split (old) | Fixed split (new) |')[1];\\n+    for (const key of ['accuracy', 'precision', 'recall', 'f1'] as const) {\\n+      const row = section.split('\\\\n').find(line => line.toLowerCase().startsWith(`| ${key} |`))?.split('|')[3];\\n+      expect(row).toContain(pitchBenchmark.model[key]);\\n+    }\\n+    const { truePositive: tp, trueNegative: tn, falsePositive: fp, falseNegative: fn } = pitchBenchmark.confusion;\\n+    expect(tp + tn + fp + fn).toBe(pitchBenchmark.testWindows);\\n+    expect(((tp + tn) / pitchBenchmark.testWindows * 100).toFixed(2) + '%').toBe(pitchBenchmark.model.accuracy);\\n+    expect((tp / (tp + fp)).toFixed(3)).toBe(pitchBenchmark.model.precision);\\n+    expect((tp / (tp + fn)).toFixed(3)).toBe(pitchBenchmark.model.recall);\\n+    expect((2 * tp / (2 * tp + fp + fn)).toFixed(3)).toBe(pitchBenchmark.model.f1);\\n+    expect(pitchBenchmark.categories.rareEvent.detected + pitchBenchmark.categories.anomaly.detected).toBe(tp);\\n+  });\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","create_time":1789292184.065587}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:28.011Z","ordinal":4451,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","session_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","root_turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","response_id":"resp_0612ff0593abfece016aa66e9723bc87d28ef7cdc3d7b6e505","usage":{"input_tokens":129471,"cached_input_tokens":122880,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1781,"reasoning_output_tokens":48,"total_tokens":131252},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":484308,"cached_input_tokens":468864,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2648,"reasoning_output_tokens":152,"total_tokens":486956},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":62524425,"cached_input_tokens":59855232,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":372526,"reasoning_output_tokens":72647,"total_tokens":62896951}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:28.463Z","ordinal":4452,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-1b083ea7-4de1-46bd-8980-de83780f3e05","changes":{"/Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission/web/src/components/evidence.tsx":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -10,5 +10,5 @@\n       <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.results[0].accuracy}</strong><span>Two-shot LLM · accuracy</span></article>\n-      <article><strong>—</strong><span>OpenTSLM · retraining pending</span></article>\n+      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.model.accuracy}</strong><span>OpenTSLM · accuracy</span></article>\n     </div>\n-    <p className=\"landing-result-note\">The evaluation now keeps each event in one split. Baselines rerun; OpenTSLM retraining pending. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\n+    <p className=\"landing-result-note\">OpenTSLM outperforms the two-shot LLM baseline. Classical summary statistics still lead at 90.18%. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\n     <div className=\"landing-next\"><Link className=\"button button-light\" href=\"/mission-control\">Open mission control <Arrow /></Link><span>Telemetry. Context. Human judgement.</span></div>\n@@ -19,4 +19,4 @@\n           <p>The two-shot frozen Llama-3.2-3B baseline reports 50.45% accuracy and 0.009 recall. Precision 1.000 accompanies extremely few positive predictions, not broad detection. F1 and a new parsing count are not reported for this rerun; the old 246-window parsing figures are not transferred to it.</p>\n-          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. Its 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 are the comparison target for the retrained OpenTSLM system. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\n-          <p>All previous fine-tuned scores were measured on the old split with cross-channel event leakage. A corrected-split OpenTSLM result is not yet available. We do not compare those old model scores against the new baselines.</p>\n+          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. It leads with 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 versus OpenTSLM at 75.89% and 0.727. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\n+          <p>OpenTSLM SP with sub-category-balanced sampling was retrained on the corrected split using an H200. It correctly classifies 170 of 224 windows: 98 nominal and 72 positive, with 14 false positives and 40 missed positive windows. Precision is 0.837, recall 0.643 and F1 0.727. Rare Event recall is 66.2% (49/74); Anomaly recall is 60.5% (23/38). These replace the old-split headline scores. Checkpoint selection used validation loss; the selected checkpoint was epoch 7.</p>\n           <p>Mission Control replays an earlier saved run on the old split (F1 0.840), not the corrected evaluation. It is a demonstration of the workflow, not evidence of new model performance. A generated rationale is a candidate aid for review, not a validated explanation.</p>\n","move_path":null},"/Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission/web/public/mission-control/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -36,3 +36,4 @@\n not the new 224-window evaluation; they must not be relabeled as fixed-split results.\n-The pitch checklist requires retraining OpenTSLM on the corrected split. Results do not establish\n+The pitch checklist now reports a retrained OpenTSLM result of 75.89% accuracy and\n+F1 0.727 on the corrected split; that separate run is not this replay. Results do not establish\n generalization to unseen events or deployment precision.\n","move_path":null},"/Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission/web/src/lib/pitch-content.ts":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -5,3 +5,5 @@\n   positiveWindows: 112,\n-  modelStatus: 'Retraining pending',\n+  model: { name: 'OpenTSLM · balanced sampling', detail: 'LoRA · retrained on the event-grouped split', accuracy: '75.89%', precision: '0.837', recall: '0.643', f1: '0.727' },\n+  confusion: { trueNegative: 98, falsePositive: 14, falseNegative: 40, truePositive: 72 },\n+  categories: { rareEvent: { detected: 49, total: 74 }, anomaly: { detected: 23, total: 38 } },\n   results: [\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM web/src/lib/pitch-content.ts\nM web/src/components/evidence.tsx\nM web/public/mission-control/README.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789292248172,"completed_at_ms":1789292248463}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:28.604Z","ordinal":4453,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-274659a1-927a-4845-b583-029756031f64","process_id":"76037","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat web/src/components/evidence.tsx"],"cwd":"file:///Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat web/src/components/evidence.tsx","name":"evidence.tsx","path":"web/src/components/evidence.tsx"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Arrow } from './brand';\nimport { pitchBenchmark } from '@/lib/pitch-content';\n\nexport function Evidence() {\n  return <section className=\"landing-evidence\" id=\"evidence\" tabIndex={-1} aria-labelledby=\"evidence-title\">\n    <div className=\"landing-evidence-heading\"><div><span className=\"eyebrow\">THE RESEARCH</span><h2 id=\"evidence-title\">Find the signal.<br /><span>Understand the context.</span></h2></div><p>ESA telemetry. Command history. OpenTSLM.<br />For the engineers behind the mission.</p></div>\n    <div className=\"landing-metrics\">\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.testWindows}</strong><span>Event-grouped test windows</span></article>\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.results[0].accuracy}</strong><span>Two-shot LLM · accuracy</span></article>\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.model.accuracy}</strong><span>OpenTSLM · accuracy</span></article>\n    </div>\n    <p className=\"landing-result-note\">OpenTSLM outperforms the two-shot LLM baseline. Classical summary statistics still lead at 90.18%. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\n    <div className=\"landing-next\"><Link className=\"button button-light\" href=\"/mission-control\">Open mission control <Arrow /></Link><span>Telemetry. Context. Human judgement.</span></div>\n    <details className=\"landing-method\"><summary>Experiment details &amp; limitations <span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary>\n      <div className=\"landing-method-body\"><table><caption>Fixed event-grouped split · 224 test windows · reported results</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Approach</th><th scope=\"col\">Accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pitchBenchmark.results.map(result => <tr key={result.name}><th scope=\"row\">{result.name}<small>{result.detail}<br />Precision {result.precision} · recall {result.recall} · F1 {result.f1 ?? 'not reported'}</small></th><td>{result.accuracy}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>\n        <div>\n          <p>The updated checklist groups all channels from the same event by anomaly_id. It reports zero event overlap across training, validation and test. The evaluation is still not strictly time-separated. The 224 test windows are balanced: 112 nominal and 112 positive. Positive means Anomaly + Rare Event.</p>\n          <p>The two-shot frozen Llama-3.2-3B baseline reports 50.45% accuracy and 0.009 recall. Precision 1.000 accompanies extremely few positive predictions, not broad detection. F1 and a new parsing count are not reported for this rerun; the old 246-window parsing figures are not transferred to it.</p>\n          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. It leads with 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 versus OpenTSLM at 75.89% and 0.727. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\n          <p>OpenTSLM SP with sub-category-balanced sampling was retrained on the corrected split using an H200. It correctly classifies 170 of 224 windows: 98 nominal and 72 positive, with 14 false positives and 40 missed positive windows. Precision is 0.837, recall 0.643 and F1 0.727. Rare Event recall is 66.2% (49/74); Anomaly recall is 60.5% (23/38). These replace the old-split headline scores. Checkpoint selection used validation loss; the selected checkpoint was epoch 7.</p>\n          <p>Mission Control replays an earlier saved run on the old split (F1 0.840), not the corrected evaluation. It is a demonstration of the workflow, not evidence of new model performance. A generated rationale is a candidate aid for review, not a validated explanation.</p>\n          <p>Source: {pitchBenchmark.source}, reproduced in the web documentation. Reported checklist results, not independently reproduced here.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n  </section>;\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Arrow } from './brand';\nimport { pitchBenchmark } from '@/lib/pitch-content';\n\nexport function Evidence() {\n  return <section className=\"landing-evidence\" id=\"evidence\" tabIndex={-1} aria-labelledby=\"evidence-title\">\n    <div className=\"landing-evidence-heading\"><div><span className=\"eyebrow\">THE RESEARCH</span><h2 id=\"evidence-title\">Find the signal.<br /><span>Understand the context.</span></h2></div><p>ESA telemetry. Command history. OpenTSLM.<br />For the engineers behind the mission.</p></div>\n    <div className=\"landing-metrics\">\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.testWindows}</strong><span>Event-grouped test windows</span></article>\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.results[0].accuracy}</strong><span>Two-shot LLM · accuracy</span></article>\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.model.accuracy}</strong><span>OpenTSLM · accuracy</span></article>\n    </div>\n    <p className=\"landing-result-note\">OpenTSLM outperforms the two-shot LLM baseline. Classical summary statistics still lead at 90.18%. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\n    <div className=\"landing-next\"><Link className=\"button button-light\" href=\"/mission-control\">Open mission control <Arrow /></Link><span>Telemetry. Context. Human judgement.</span></div>\n    <details className=\"landing-method\"><summary>Experiment details &amp; limitations <span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary>\n      <div className=\"landing-method-body\"><table><caption>Fixed event-grouped split · 224 test windows · reported results</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Approach</th><th scope=\"col\">Accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pitchBenchmark.results.map(result => <tr key={result.name}><th scope=\"row\">{result.name}<small>{result.detail}<br />Precision {result.precision} · recall {result.recall} · F1 {result.f1 ?? 'not reported'}</small></th><td>{result.accuracy}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>\n        <div>\n          <p>The updated checklist groups all channels from the same event by anomaly_id. It reports zero event overlap across training, validation and test. The evaluation is still not strictly time-separated. The 224 test windows are balanced: 112 nominal and 112 positive. Positive means Anomaly + Rare Event.</p>\n          <p>The two-shot frozen Llama-3.2-3B baseline reports 50.45% accuracy and 0.009 recall. Precision 1.000 accompanies extremely few positive predictions, not broad detection. F1 and a new parsing count are not reported for this rerun; the old 246-window parsing figures are not transferred to it.</p>\n          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. It leads with 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 versus OpenTSLM at 75.89% and 0.727. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\n          <p>OpenTSLM SP with sub-category-balanced sampling was retrained on the corrected split using an H200. It correctly classifies 170 of 224 windows: 98 nominal and 72 positive, with 14 false positives and 40 missed positive windows. Precision is 0.837, recall 0.643 and F1 0.727. Rare Event recall is 66.2% (49/74); Anomaly recall is 60.5% (23/38). These replace the old-split headline scores. Checkpoint selection used validation loss; the selected checkpoint was epoch 7.</p>\n          <p>Mission Control replays an earlier saved run on the old split (F1 0.840), not the corrected evaluation. It is a demonstration of the workflow, not evidence of new model performance. A generated rationale is a candidate aid for review, not a validated explanation.</p>\n          <p>Source: {pitchBenchmark.source}, reproduced in the web documentation. Reported checklist results, not independently reproduced here.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n  </section>;\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":1000},"formatted_output":"import Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Arrow } from './brand';\nimport { pitchBenchmark } from '@/lib/pitch-content';\n\nexport function Evidence() {\n  return <section className=\"landing-evidence\" id=\"evidence\" tabIndex={-1} aria-labelledby=\"evidence-title\">\n    <div className=\"landing-evidence-heading\"><div><span className=\"eyebrow\">THE RESEARCH</span><h2 id=\"evidence-title\">Find the signal.<br /><span>Understand the context.</span></h2></div><p>ESA telemetry. Command history. OpenTSLM.<br />For the engineers behind the mission.</p></div>\n    <div className=\"landing-metrics\">\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.testWindows}</strong><span>Event-grouped test windows</span></article>\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.results[0].accuracy}</strong><span>Two-shot LLM · accuracy</span></article>\n      <article><strong>{pitchBenchmark.model.accuracy}</strong><span>OpenTSLM · accuracy</span></article>\n    </div>\n    <p className=\"landing-result-note\">OpenTSLM outperforms the two-shot LLM baseline. Classical summary statistics still lead at 90.18%. Reported results — not flight validation.</p>\n    <div className=\"landing-next\"><Link className=\"button button-light\" href=\"/mission-control\">Open mission control <Arrow /></Link><span>Telemetry. Context. Human judgement.</span></div>\n    <details className=\"landing-method\"><summary>Experiment details &amp; limitations <span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary>\n      <div className=\"landing-method-body\"><table><caption>Fixed event-grouped split · 224 test windows · reported results</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Approach</th><th scope=\"col\">Accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pitchBenchmark.results.map(result => <tr key={result.name}><th scope=\"row\">{result.name}<small>{result.detail}<br />Precision {result.precision} · recall {result.recall} · F1 {result.f1 ?? 'not reported'}</small></th><td>{result.accuracy}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>\n        <div>\n          <p>The updated checklist groups all channels from the same event by anomaly_id. It reports zero event overlap across training, validation and test. The evaluation is still not strictly time-separated. The 224 test windows are balanced: 112 nominal and 112 positive. Positive means Anomaly + Rare Event.</p>\n          <p>The two-shot frozen Llama-3.2-3B baseline reports 50.45% accuracy and 0.009 recall. Precision 1.000 accompanies extremely few positive predictions, not broad detection. F1 and a new parsing count are not reported for this rerun; the old 246-window parsing figures are not transferred to it.</p>\n          <p>The restricted classical baseline uses mean, standard deviation and telecommand presence/timing. It leads with 90.18% accuracy and 0.891 F1 versus OpenTSLM at 75.89% and 0.727. The five-feature and raw-values baselines use different input representations, so this is not an isolated measure of encoder performance.</p>\n          <p>OpenTSLM SP with sub-category-balanced sampling was retrained on the corrected split using an H200. It correctly classifies 170 of 224 windows: 98 nominal and 72 positive, with 14 false positives and 40 missed positive windows. Precision is 0.837, recall 0.643 and F1 0.727. Rare Event recall is 66.2% (49/74); Anomaly recall is 60.5% (23/38). These replace the old-split headline scores. Checkpoint selection used validation loss; the selected checkpoint was epoch 7.</p>\n          <p>Mission Control replays an earlier saved run on the old split (F1 0.840), not the corrected evaluation. It is a demonstration of the workflow, not evidence of new model performance. A generated rationale is a candidate aid for review, not a validated explanation.</p>\n          <p>Source: {pitchBenchmark.source}, reproduced in the web documentation. Reported checklist results, not independently reproduced here.</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </details>\n  </section>;\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1789292248604,"completed_at_ms":1789292248604}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:28.787Z","ordinal":4454,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-e19326ae-2b8e-4caa-9129-f690caaa317b","changes":{"/Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission/web/src/components/evidence.tsx":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -15,3 +15,3 @@\n     <details className=\"landing-method\"><summary>Experiment details &amp; limitations <span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary>\n-      <div className=\"landing-method-body\"><table><caption>Fixed event-grouped split · 224 test windows · reported results</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Approach</th><th scope=\"col\">Accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pitchBenchmark.results.map(result => <tr key={result.name}><th scope=\"row\">{result.name}<small>{result.detail}<br />Precision {result.precision} · recall {result.recall} · F1 {result.f1 ?? 'not reported'}</small></th><td>{result.accuracy}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>\n+      <div className=\"landing-method-body\"><table><caption>Fixed event-grouped split · 224 test windows · reported results</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Approach</th><th scope=\"col\">Accuracy</th></tr></thead><tbody>{[pitchBenchmark.model, ...pitchBenchmark.results].map(result => <tr key={result.name}><th scope=\"row\">{result.name}<small>{result.detail}<br />Precision {result.precision} · recall {result.recall} · F1 {result.f1 ?? 'not reported'}</small></th><td>{result.accuracy}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>\n         <div>\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM web/src/components/evidence.tsx\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1789292248690,"completed_at_ms":1789292248787}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:28.924Z","ordinal":4455,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6d112303-b9a4-4235-afb3-630fb2222ddf","process_id":"26131","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat web/tests/experience.spec.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat web/tests/experience.spec.ts","name":"experience.spec.ts","path":"web/tests/experience.spec.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';\n\ntest('minimal cinematic journey keeps dramatic copy and optional scene controls', async ({ page }) => {\n  const errors: string[] = [];\n  page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(error.message));\n  await page.goto('/');\n  await expect(page.locator('#descent')).toHaveAttribute('data-ready', 'true');\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Years of work. One mission.' })).toBeInViewport();\n  await expect(page.locator('.landing .brand')).toHaveCount(0);\n  await expect(page.locator('.landing-header a')).toHaveCount(1);\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pause ambient animation' })).not.toBeVisible();\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/orbit-desktop.png' });\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Atmospheric re-entry', exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Then everything changes.' })).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.waitForTimeout(400);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/reentry-desktop.png' });\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Enable atmospheric sound' }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Mute atmospheric sound' })).toHaveAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Mute atmospheric sound' }).click();\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pause ambient animation' }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Resume ambient animation' })).toHaveAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Protect the mission', exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'An anomaly shouldn’t end a mission.' })).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.locator('[data-chapter=\"0\"]')).toHaveAttribute('inert', '');\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/final-desktop.png' });\n  expect(errors).toEqual([]);\n});\n\ntest('three checklist figures remain honest with expandable methodology', async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.goto('/#evidence');\n  const evidence = page.locator('#evidence');\n  await expect(evidence.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Find the signal. Understand the context.' })).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(evidence.locator('.landing-metrics article')).toHaveCount(3);\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('OpenTSLM retraining pending');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('not flight validation');\n  await expect(evidence.getByRole('table')).not.toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.locator('#approach, .pitch-window-preview, .brand')).toHaveCount(0);\n  await evidence.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/evidence-desktop.png' });\n  await page.getByText('Experiment details & limitations', { exact: false }).click();\n  await expect(evidence.getByRole('table')).toBeVisible();\n  for (const [name, accuracy] of [['Two-shot Llama-3.2-3B', '50.45%'], ['Classical · current prompt features', '90.18%'], ['Classical · five engineered features', '92.86%'], ['Classical · raw values only', '57.59%']]) {\n    await expect(evidence.getByRole('row').filter({ hasText: name })).toContainText(accuracy);\n  }\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('not strictly time-separated');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('112 nominal and 112 positive');\n  await expect(evidence).not.toContainText('68 of 69');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('F1 and a new parsing count are not reported');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('extremely few positive predictions');\n  await expect(evidence).not.toContainText('23.6%');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('not an isolated measure');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('not a validated explanation');\n  await expect(evidence).toContainText('Docs/PITCH_REQUIREMENTS_CHECKLIST.md');\n  await evidence.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/methodology-desktop.png' });\n});\n\ntest('mobile reduced-motion journey and keyboard skip link remain usable', async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 390, height: 844 });\n  await page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'reduce' });\n  await page.goto('/');\n  await expect(page.locator('#descent')).toHaveAttribute('data-ready', 'true');\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/orbit-mobile.png' });\n  await page.keyboard.press('Tab');\n  await expect(page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Skip the cinematic experience' })).toBeFocused();\n  await page.keyboard.press('Enter');\n  await expect(page.locator('#evidence')).toBeFocused();\n  await page.locator('#evidence').screenshot({ path: 'test-results/evidence-mobile.png' });\n  expect(await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth)).toBe(true);\n  await page.goto('/');\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Resume ambient animation' })).toHaveAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Protect the mission', exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'An anomaly shouldn’t end a mission.' })).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/final-mobile.png' });\n  expect(await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= innerWidth)).toBe(true);\n});\n\ntest('landing links to Mission Control without initiating inference; clean film is unchanged', async ({ page, request }) => {\n  const jobs: string[] = [];\n  page.on('request', req => { if (req.url().includes('/api/pipeline/jobs')) jobs.push(req.url()); });\n  await page.goto('/');\n  await expect(page.locator('.landing-header a')).toHaveAttribute('href', '/mission-control');\n  await expect(page.locator('#evidence').getByRole('link', { name: 'Open mission control' })).toHaveAttribute('href', '/mission-control');\n  await expect(page.locator('video, #film-dialog')).toHaveCount(0);\n  const film = await page.getByRole('link', { name: 'Download text-free video' }).getAttribute('href');\n  expect(film).toBe('/films/perigee-descent-clean.mp4');\n  expect((await request.head(film!)).status()).toBe(200);\n  await expect(page.locator('#scene-description')).toContainText('not an orbital simulation');\n  expect(jobs).toEqual([]);\n});\n\ntest('WebGL fallback preserves the dramatic headline and research', async ({ page }) => {\n  await page.addInitScript(() => {\n    const getContext = HTMLCanvasElement.prototype.getContext;\n    HTMLCanvasElement.prototype.getContext = function (this: HTMLCanvasElement, type: string, ...args: unknown[]) {\n      if (type.startsWith('webgl')) return null;\n      return Reflect.apply(getContext, this, [type, ...args]);\n    } as typeof getContext;\n  });\n  await page.goto('/');\n  await expect(page.locator('.flight-stage')).toHaveClass(/static-fallback/);\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Years of work. One mission.' })).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.locator('#evidence')).toContainText('50.45%');\n  await expect(page.locator('#evidence')).not.toContainText('86.99%');\n});\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';\n\ntest('minimal cinematic journey keeps dramatic copy and optional scene controls', async ({ page }) => {\n  const errors: string[] = [];\n  page.on('pageerror', error => errors.push(error.message));\n  await page.goto('/');\n  await expect(page.locator('#descent')).toHaveAttribute('data-ready', 'true');\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Years of work. One mission.' })).toBeInViewport();\n  await expect(page.locator('.landing .brand')).toHaveCount(0);\n  await expect(page.locator('.landing-header a')).toHaveCount(1);\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pause ambient animation' })).not.toBeVisible();\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/orbit-desktop.png' });\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Atmospheric re-entry', exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Then everything changes.' })).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.waitForTimeout(400);\n  await page.screenshot({ path: 'test-results/reentry-desktop.png' });\n  await page.getByText('Scene controls', { exact: true }).click();\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Enable atmospheric sound' }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Mute atmospheric sound' })).toHaveAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Mute atmospheric sound' }).click();\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pause ambient animation' }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Resume ambient animation' })).toHaveAttribute('aria-pressed', 'true');\n  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Protect the mission', exact: true }).click();\n  await expect(page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'An anomaly shouldn’t end a mission.' })).toBeVisible();\n  awa