{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:37.587Z","ordinal":4470,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","session_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","root_turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","response_id":"resp_0612ff0593abfece016aa66edb413887d28f8d81cfb389255e","usage":{"input_tokens":131282,"cached_input_tokens":129280,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":148,"reasoning_output_tokens":13,"total_tokens":131430},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":615590,"cached_input_tokens":598144,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2796,"reasoning_output_tokens":165,"total_tokens":618386},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":62655707,"cached_input_tokens":59984512,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":372674,"reasoning_output_tokens":72660,"total_tokens":63028381}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:37.692Z","ordinal":4471,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a09554-4029-7852-babe-0cbdfd76c3e6","turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2d11201f-fcf1-41fe-a2dc-9aaf3d5e75fd","process_id":"39896","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat /Users/luisdehlwes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/presentations/26.630.12135/skills/presentations/artifact_tool/API_QUICK_START.md /Users/luisdehlwes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/presentations/26.630.12135/skills/presentations/artifact_tool/api/API_DOCS.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/luisdehlwes/Developer/02_events/04_zurich/ehl-zurich-hackathon-submission","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat /Users/luisdehlwes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/presentations/26.630.12135/skills/presentations/artifact_tool/API_QUICK_START.md /Users/luisdehlwes/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/presentations/26.630.12135/skills/presentations/artifact_tool/api/API_DOCS.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Presentation Quick Start (TypeScript)\n\n## API Docs\n\nAPI docs: `api/API_DOCS.md`\n\n`Presentation` is the in-memory API object. A deck is the exported presentation\nfile. A slide is one page in the deck.\n\n## Imports\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { FileBlob, Presentation, PresentationFile } from \"@oai/artifact-tool\";\n```\n\n## Create, Render, Export\n\nThis script creates an editable deck, renders each slide PNG, writes each slide\nlayout JSON, writes a deck montage with `montage: true`, and exports PPTX.\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { Presentation, PresentationFile } from \"@oai/artifact-tool\";\n\nasync function writeBlob(path: string, blob: Blob): Promise<void> {\n  await fs.writeFile(path, new Uint8Array(await blob.arrayBuffer()));\n}\n\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  await fs.mkdir(\"output\", { recursive: true });\n\n  const presentation = Presentation.create({\n    slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n  });\n\n  const slide = presentation.slides.add();\n  slide.background.fill = \"slate-50\";\n\n  const page = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\n  const gutter = 28;\n  const leftCol = 430;\n  const rightCol = page.width - leftCol - gutter;\n\n  const eyebrow = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: { left: page.left, top: page.top, width: 280, height: 28 },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  eyebrow.text = \"EDITABLE PRESENTATION\";\n  eyebrow.text.style = { fontSize: 12, bold: true, color: \"slate-500\" };\n\n  const title = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left,\n      top: page.top + 92,\n      width: leftCol,\n      height: 184,\n    },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  title.text = \"Build decks with editable objects\";\n  title.text.style = { fontSize: 42, bold: true, color: \"slate-950\" };\n\n  const subtitle = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left,\n      top: page.top + 292,\n      width: leftCol,\n      height: 96,\n    },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  subtitle.text =\n    \"Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain editable.\";\n  subtitle.text.style = { fontSize: 20, color: \"slate-600\" };\n\n  const chartFrame = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"roundRect\",\n    name: \"chart-frame\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left + leftCol + gutter,\n      top: page.top + 92,\n      width: rightCol,\n      height: 388,\n    },\n    fill: \"white\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n    borderRadius: \"rounded-2xl\",\n    shadow: \"shadow-sm\",\n  });\n\n  slide.charts.add(\"bar\", {\n    position: {\n      left: chartFrame.position.left + 36,\n      top: chartFrame.position.top + 52,\n      width: chartFrame.position.width - 72,\n      height: 280,\n    },\n    categories: [\"Rows\", \"Grid\", \"Tokens\"],\n    series: [{ name: \"Coverage\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \"accent1\" }],\n    hasLegend: false,\n    dataLabels: { showValue: true, position: \"outEnd\" },\n    yAxis: {\n      majorGridlines: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n    },\n  });\n\n  for (const [index, slide] of presentation.slides.items.entries()) {\n    const stem = `slide-${String(index + 1).padStart(2, \"0\")}`;\n    const png = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\n    await writeBlob(`output/${stem}.png`, png);\n\n    const layout = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\n    await fs.writeFile(`output/${stem}.layout.json`, await layout.text());\n  }\n\n  const montage = await presentation.export({\n    format: \"webp\",\n    montage: true,\n    scale: 1,\n  });\n  await writeBlob(\"output/deck-montage.webp\", montage);\n\n  const pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\n  await pptx.save(\"output/deck.pptx\");\n}\n\nmain().catch((error) => {\n  console.error(error);\n  process.exitCode = 1;\n});\n```\n\n## JSX Compose Equivalent\n\nUse JSX when the slide is naturally rows, columns, grids, or overlays.\n\n```tsx\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\n/** @jsxImportSource @oai/artifact-tool/presentation-jsx */\n\nconst frame = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\n\nslide.compose(\n  <column name=\"content-frame\" width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28}>\n    <row width=\"fill\" height={72} align=\"center\" justify=\"between\">\n      <paragraph name=\"eyebrow\" className=\"text-slate-500 text-sm font-bold\">\n        EDITABLE PRESENTATION\n      </paragraph>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">Q2 planning</paragraph>\n    </row>\n    <row width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28} align=\"stretch\">\n      <column width={430} height=\"fill\" gap={18}>\n        <paragraph\n          name=\"primary-heading\"\n          className=\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\"\n        >\n          Build decks with editable objects\n        </paragraph>\n        <paragraph className=\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\">\n          Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain\n          editable.\n        </paragraph>\n      </column>\n      <box\n        name=\"chart-frame\"\n        width=\"fill\"\n        height=\"fill\"\n        className=\"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm\"\n        line={{ style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 }}\n      >\n        <chart\n          name=\"coverage-chart\"\n          chartType=\"bar\"\n          categories={[\"Rows\", \"Grid\", \"Tokens\"]}\n          series={[{ name: \"Coverage\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \"accent1\" }]}\n          hasLegend={false}\n          width=\"fill\"\n          height=\"fill\"\n        />\n      </box>\n    </row>\n  </column>,\n  { frame, baseUnit: 8 },\n);\n```\n\n## Import And Edit PPTX\n\nLoad a PPTX, inspect for stable ids, render before/after evidence, make a\nfocused edit, re-inspect, and export the edited PPTX.\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = await PresentationFile.importPptx(\n  await FileBlob.load(\"input.pptx\"),\n);\n\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\",\n  search: \"Revenue\",\n  maxChars: 8000,\n});\nconsole.log(before.ndjson);\n\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideIdFromInspect);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/before-slide.png\",\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 }),\n);\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  \"output/before-slide.layout.json\",\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })).text(),\n);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/before-montage.webp\",\n  await presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\n);\n\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\ntarget.text.replace(\"Revenue\", \"Updated revenue outlook\");\n\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/after-slide.png\",\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 }),\n);\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  \"output/after-slide.layout.json\",\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })).text(),\n);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/after-montage.webp\",\n  await presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\n);\n\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\n  kind: \"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\",\n  maxChars: 3000,\n});\nconsole.log(after.ndjson);\n\nconst pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\nawait pptx.save(\"output/edited-deck.pptx\");\n```\n\n## Local Image Bytes\n\nUse byte-backed images for embedded PPTX assets.\n\n```ts\nasync function readImageBlob(imagePath: string): Promise<ArrayBuffer> {\n  const bytes = await fs.readFile(imagePath);\n  return bytes.buffer.slice(\n    bytes.byteOffset,\n    bytes.byteOffset + bytes.byteLength,\n  );\n}\n\nconst imageBytes = await readImageBlob(\"assets/product.png\");\nslide.images.add({\n  blob: imageBytes,\n  contentType: \"image/png\",\n  alt: \"Product screenshot\",\n  fit: \"cover\",\n  position: { left: 720, top: 96, width: 420, height: 280 },\n  geometry: \"roundRect\",\n  borderRadius: \"rounded-xl\",\n});\n```\n# Presentation API Docs\n\nUse the presentation facades to create PowerPoint-style decks in TypeScript.\n\n## Conventions (units + presets)\n\n- **Pixels everywhere**: all slide geometry uses CSS pixels (`px`) at 96 DPI: `position.{left,top,width,height}`, line widths, and text `fontSize`.\n- **Default canvas for examples**: use `1280 x 720` unless the task or source deck says otherwise. A useful full-slide content frame is `{ left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 }`.\n- **Angles**: rotations use degrees.\n- **Preset geometry**: `geometry` uses preset shape-name strings. Use standard shape presets and `geometry: \"custom\"` for bespoke paths.\n- **Gradients**: stop `offset` ranges from `0` to `100000`.\n- **Config-first authoring**: pass config objects into create/add APIs and grouped setters when the API provides them.\n- **String values**: options such as geometry, fit, alignment, chart type, line style, and connector kind are strings; reference pages list exact small unions and grep targets for huge catalogs.\n- **Inline docs types**: reference pages include illustrative `type ... = { ... }` blocks. Treat them as schema-shaped authoring guidance, not imports.\n- **Authoring surfaces**: `slide.compose(...)` covers rows, columns, grids, layers, and token strings. Config-first facade APIs cover exact positions, fixed chrome, native charts/tables/images, and imported deck edits.\n\n## Common Routes\n\n- Rows, columns, grids, overlays, and 12-column spans: [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md).\n- JSX node props and sizing mechanics: [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md).\n- Tailwind-like visual strings: [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md).\n- Inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops: [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md).\n\n## Quick start\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n});\n\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\nslide.background.fill = \"slate-50\";\n\nconst headline = slide.shapes.add({\n  geometry: \"textbox\",\n  name: \"headline\",\n  position: { left: 72, top: 64, width: 720, height: 96 },\n  fill: \"none\",\n  line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n});\nheadline.text = \"Editable headline\";\nheadline.text.style = { fontSize: 44, bold: true, color: \"slate-950\" };\n\nconst shape = slide.shapes.add({\n  geometry: \"roundRect\",\n  name: \"summary-surface\",\n  position: { left: 72, top: 188, width: 520, height: 300 },\n  fill: \"white\",\n  line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n  borderRadius: \"rounded-2xl\",\n});\n\nconst previewBlob = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 2 });\nconst layoutBlob = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\nconst montageBlob = await presentation.export({\n  format: \"webp\",\n  montage: true,\n  scale: 1,\n});\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape\",\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst help = presentation.help(\"*\", {\n  search: \"chart axis labels\",\n  include: [\"index\", \"notes\"],\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n## Load Existing Presentation Data\n\nUse `Presentation.load(proto)` when a host adapter gives the library serialized\npresentation data. The loaded object exposes the same inspect, resolve, edit,\nrender, and serialize APIs as a newly created presentation.\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = Presentation.load(proto);\n\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\",\n  search: \"Revenue\",\n  maxChars: 8000,\n});\n\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideAnchorIdFromInspect);\nconst previewBefore = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst layoutBefore = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\n\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\ntarget.text.replace(\"Revenue\", \"Revenue outlook\");\ntarget.text.style = { fontSize: 24, color: \"slate-950\", bold: true };\n\nconst previewAfter = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst layoutAfter = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\n  kind: \"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\",\n  maxChars: 3000,\n});\nconst nextProto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n## Compose-first layout\n\n```tsx\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\n\nconst presentation = Presentation.create();\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\n\nslide.compose(\n  <column width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={16}>\n    <paragraph name=\"headline\" className=\"text-slate-950 text-3xl leading-tight\">\n      <run textStyle={{ bold: true }}>Quarterly</run>\n      <run> readiness</run>\n    </paragraph>\n    <rule stroke=\"#0f172a\" width={160} weight={2} />\n  </column>,\n  {\n    frame: { left: 48, top: 40, width: 864, height: 460 },\n    baseUnit: 8,\n  },\n);\n```\n\nUse `name` for stable inspect and layout-export targeting. JSX materializing\ntags default `width` to `\"fill\"` when you omit it.\n\n## Core API Sequence\n\n- Create presentations with `Presentation.create({ slideSize })` to control default slide dimensions.\n- Add slides with `presentation.slides.add({ layout, layoutId })` or `presentation.slides.insert({ after, ... })`.\n- Use `slide.compose(nodeOrJsx, { frame, baseUnit })` for compose-first layouts. JSX lowers into the same compose runtime as the helper-based API.\n- Author content with config-first calls: `slide.shapes.add({ geometry, position, fill, line })`, `slide.images.add({ ... })`, `slide.tables.add({ ... })`, and `slide.charts.add(chartType, { ... })`.\n- Format whole-shape text with grouped configs such as `shape.text.style = { fontSize, bold, color, alignment }`.\n- Edit imported decks with `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })`, `presentation.resolve(anchorId)`, and focused facade edits.\n- Export previews with `presentation.export({ slide, format, scale })`.\n- Export deck montages with `presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 })`.\n- Export layout JSON with `slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })`.\n- Search API help with `presentation.help(query, { search, include, maxChars })`.\n- Run high-level edits with `presentation.scripts.run(kind, options)`; see [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) for the script surface.\n\n## Output Map\n\n| Output | API | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slide PNG | `presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale })` | One preview image for one slide |\n| Deck montage | `presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale })` | One overview image containing the deck slides |\n| Layout JSON | `slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })` | Structural JSON with bounds, ids, text, names, and object metadata |\n| Searchable snapshot | `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })` | NDJSON records for locating and resolving objects |\n| Runtime handoff | `presentation.toProto()` | Serializable presentation data for host adapters |\n\n## Minimal Patterns\n\nUse these as the first API patterns to reach for:\n\n```ts\n// Create, preview, inspect, then serialize.\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n});\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\nconst preview = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst montage = await presentation.export({\n  format: \"webp\",\n  montage: true,\n  scale: 1,\n});\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,chart,table\",\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n```tsx\n// Compose structure with first-principles rows/columns.\nslide.compose(\n  <row width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28}>\n    <column width={420} height=\"fill\" gap={16}>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\">\n        Title\n      </paragraph>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\">\n        Editable copy in a fixed text column.\n      </paragraph>\n    </column>\n    <box\n      width=\"fill\"\n      height=\"fill\"\n      className=\"bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl shadow-sm\"\n    />\n  </row>,\n  { frame: { left: 56, top: 56, width: 1168, height: 608 }, baseUnit: 8 },\n);\n```\n\nFor 3-column and 12-column layouts, use [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md); keep spans local with `{ mode: \"fr\", value: 1 }` track objects.\n\nUse `className` only for visual/text tokens such as `bg-*`, `rounded-*`,\n`shadow-*`, `text-*`, `font-*`, and `leading-*`. Use layout props for\n`width`, `height`, `gap`, `padding`, `align`, and `justify`.\n\n## Reference Map\n\nOpen these references as needed:\n\n- [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md) — compact JSX node surface and layout mechanics.\n- [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md) — Tailwind-like token reference for colors, text, radius, shadows, and `className`.\n- [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md) — first-principles layout recipes for rows, columns, 12-column grids, alignment, masks, and overlays.\n- [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md) — safe inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops for existing decks.\n- [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) — `Presentation` facade, slide collection, export/toProto, scripts.\n- [`references/slide.spec.md`](./references/slide.spec.md) — `Slide` API, backgrounds, placeholders, notes, export, auto-layout.\n- [`references/inspect.md`](./references/inspect.md) — grep-first snapshot (`inspect → rg → resolve/edit → re-inspect`) for loaded presentation data and templates.\n- [`references/help.md`](./references/help.md) — grep-first API and template lookup (`help → build/edit → inspect`) for presentation JS workflows.\n- [`references/layout.spec.md`](./references/layout.spec.md) — layouts, placeholders, and slide layout assignment.\n- [`references/master.spec.md`](./references/master.spec.md) — masters, layout linking, background refs, color maps.\n- [`references/theme.spec.md`](./references/theme.spec.md) — theme color schemes and hex maps.\n- [`references/styles.spec.md`](./references/styles.spec.md) — named text styles and flow through text.\n- [`references/rich-text.spec.md`](./references/rich-text.spec.md) — text blocks, ranges, links, list presets.\n- [`references/shapes.spec.md`](./references/shapes.spec.md) — shape geometry, fills, strokes, rounded corners, shadows, and z-ordering.\n- [`references/connectors.md`](./references/connectors.md) — connected lines, arrows, side anchors, direct connection sites, and rerouting behavior.\n- [`references/fill.spec.md`](./references/fill.spec.md) — fill/stroke config shapes and color shorthands, solid, gradient, pattern.\n- [`references/images.spec.md`](./references/images.spec.md) — images, cropping, contain/cover framing, prompt placeholders.\n- [`references/tables.spec.md`](./references/tables.spec.md) — tables, merges, and cell text.\n- [`references/charts.spec.md`](./references/charts.spec.md) — charts, series, axes, legends, mini-chart YAML.\n- [`references/comments.md`](./references/comments.md) — comment authors, threads, replies, reactions, and resolving imported review threads.\n- [`references/auto-layout.spec.md`](./references/auto-layout.spec.md) — deterministic layout helpers for arranging shapes within frames.\n- [`references/speaker-notes.spec.md`](./references/speaker-notes.spec.md) — speaker notes surface and visibility toggles.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Presentation Quick Start (TypeScript)\n\n## API Docs\n\nAPI docs: `api/API_DOCS.md`\n\n`Presentation` is the in-memory API object. A deck is the exported presentation\nfile. A slide is one page in the deck.\n\n## Imports\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { FileBlob, Presentation, PresentationFile } from \"@oai/artifact-tool\";\n```\n\n## Create, Render, Export\n\nThis script creates an editable deck, renders each slide PNG, writes each slide\nlayout JSON, writes a deck montage with `montage: true`, and exports PPTX.\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { Presentation, PresentationFile } from \"@oai/artifact-tool\";\n\nasync function writeBlob(path: string, blob: Blob): Promise<void> {\n  await fs.writeFile(path, new Uint8Array(await blob.arrayBuffer()));\n}\n\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  await fs.mkdir(\"output\", { recursive: true });\n\n  const presentation = Presentation.create({\n    slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n  });\n\n  const slide = presentation.slides.add();\n  slide.background.fill = \"slate-50\";\n\n  const page = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\n  const gutter = 28;\n  const leftCol = 430;\n  const rightCol = page.width - leftCol - gutter;\n\n  const eyebrow = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: { left: page.left, top: page.top, width: 280, height: 28 },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  eyebrow.text = \"EDITABLE PRESENTATION\";\n  eyebrow.text.style = { fontSize: 12, bold: true, color: \"slate-500\" };\n\n  const title = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left,\n      top: page.top + 92,\n      width: leftCol,\n      height: 184,\n    },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  title.text = \"Build decks with editable objects\";\n  title.text.style = { fontSize: 42, bold: true, color: \"slate-950\" };\n\n  const subtitle = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left,\n      top: page.top + 292,\n      width: leftCol,\n      height: 96,\n    },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  subtitle.text =\n    \"Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain editable.\";\n  subtitle.text.style = { fontSize: 20, color: \"slate-600\" };\n\n  const chartFrame = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"roundRect\",\n    name: \"chart-frame\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left + leftCol + gutter,\n      top: page.top + 92,\n      width: rightCol,\n      height: 388,\n    },\n    fill: \"white\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n    borderRadius: \"rounded-2xl\",\n    shadow: \"shadow-sm\",\n  });\n\n  slide.charts.add(\"bar\", {\n    position: {\n      left: chartFrame.position.left + 36,\n      top: chartFrame.position.top + 52,\n      width: chartFrame.position.width - 72,\n      height: 280,\n    },\n    categories: [\"Rows\", \"Grid\", \"Tokens\"],\n    series: [{ name: \"Coverage\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \"accent1\" }],\n    hasLegend: false,\n    dataLabels: { showValue: true, position: \"outEnd\" },\n    yAxis: {\n      majorGridlines: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n    },\n  });\n\n  for (const [index, slide] of presentation.slides.items.entries()) {\n    const stem = `slide-${String(index + 1).padStart(2, \"0\")}`;\n    const png = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\n    await writeBlob(`output/${stem}.png`, png);\n\n    const layout = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\n    await fs.writeFile(`output/${stem}.layout.json`, await layout.text());\n  }\n\n  const montage = await presentation.export({\n    format: \"webp\",\n    montage: true,\n    scale: 1,\n  });\n  await writeBlob(\"output/deck-montage.webp\", montage);\n\n  const pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\n  await pptx.save(\"output/deck.pptx\");\n}\n\nmain().catch((error) => {\n  console.error(error);\n  process.exitCode = 1;\n});\n```\n\n## JSX Compose Equivalent\n\nUse JSX when the slide is naturally rows, columns, grids, or overlays.\n\n```tsx\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\n/** @jsxImportSource @oai/artifact-tool/presentation-jsx */\n\nconst frame = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\n\nslide.compose(\n  <column name=\"content-frame\" width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28}>\n    <row width=\"fill\" height={72} align=\"center\" justify=\"between\">\n      <paragraph name=\"eyebrow\" className=\"text-slate-500 text-sm font-bold\">\n        EDITABLE PRESENTATION\n      </paragraph>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">Q2 planning</paragraph>\n    </row>\n    <row width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28} align=\"stretch\">\n      <column width={430} height=\"fill\" gap={18}>\n        <paragraph\n          name=\"primary-heading\"\n          className=\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\"\n        >\n          Build decks with editable objects\n        </paragraph>\n        <paragraph className=\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\">\n          Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain\n          editable.\n        </paragraph>\n      </column>\n      <box\n        name=\"chart-frame\"\n        width=\"fill\"\n        height=\"fill\"\n        className=\"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm\"\n        line={{ style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 }}\n      >\n        <chart\n          name=\"coverage-chart\"\n          chartType=\"bar\"\n          categories={[\"Rows\", \"Grid\", \"Tokens\"]}\n          series={[{ name: \"Coverage\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \"accent1\" }]}\n          hasLegend={false}\n          width=\"fill\"\n          height=\"fill\"\n        />\n      </box>\n    </row>\n  </column>,\n  { frame, baseUnit: 8 },\n);\n```\n\n## Import And Edit PPTX\n\nLoad a PPTX, inspect for stable ids, render before/after evidence, make a\nfocused edit, re-inspect, and export the edited PPTX.\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = await PresentationFile.importPptx(\n  await FileBlob.load(\"input.pptx\"),\n);\n\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\",\n  search: \"Revenue\",\n  maxChars: 8000,\n});\nconsole.log(before.ndjson);\n\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideIdFromInspect);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/before-slide.png\",\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 }),\n);\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  \"output/before-slide.layout.json\",\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })).text(),\n);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/before-montage.webp\",\n  await presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\n);\n\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\ntarget.text.replace(\"Revenue\", \"Updated revenue outlook\");\n\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/after-slide.png\",\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 }),\n);\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  \"output/after-slide.layout.json\",\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })).text(),\n);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/after-montage.webp\",\n  await presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\n);\n\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\n  kind: \"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\",\n  maxChars: 3000,\n});\nconsole.log(after.ndjson);\n\nconst pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\nawait pptx.save(\"output/edited-deck.pptx\");\n```\n\n## Local Image Bytes\n\nUse byte-backed images for embedded PPTX assets.\n\n```ts\nasync function readImageBlob(imagePath: string): Promise<ArrayBuffer> {\n  const bytes = await fs.readFile(imagePath);\n  return bytes.buffer.slice(\n    bytes.byteOffset,\n    bytes.byteOffset + bytes.byteLength,\n  );\n}\n\nconst imageBytes = await readImageBlob(\"assets/product.png\");\nslide.images.add({\n  blob: imageBytes,\n  contentType: \"image/png\",\n  alt: \"Product screenshot\",\n  fit: \"cover\",\n  position: { left: 720, top: 96, width: 420, height: 280 },\n  geometry: \"roundRect\",\n  borderRadius: \"rounded-xl\",\n});\n```\n# Presentation API Docs\n\nUse the presentation facades to create PowerPoint-style decks in TypeScript.\n\n## Conventions (units + presets)\n\n- **Pixels everywhere**: all slide geometry uses CSS pixels (`px`) at 96 DPI: `position.{left,top,width,height}`, line widths, and text `fontSize`.\n- **Default canvas for examples**: use `1280 x 720` unless the task or source deck says otherwise. A useful full-slide content frame is `{ left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 }`.\n- **Angles**: rotations use degrees.\n- **Preset geometry**: `geometry` uses preset shape-name strings. Use standard shape presets and `geometry: \"custom\"` for bespoke paths.\n- **Gradients**: stop `offset` ranges from `0` to `100000`.\n- **Config-first authoring**: pass config objects into create/add APIs and grouped setters when the API provides them.\n- **String values**: options such as geometry, fit, alignment, chart type, line style, and connector kind are strings; reference pages list exact small unions and grep targets for huge catalogs.\n- **Inline docs types**: reference pages include illustrative `type ... = { ... }` blocks. Treat them as schema-shaped authoring guidance, not imports.\n- **Authoring surfaces**: `slide.compose(...)` covers rows, columns, grids, layers, and token strings. Config-first facade APIs cover exact positions, fixed chrome, native charts/tables/images, and imported deck edits.\n\n## Common Routes\n\n- Rows, columns, grids, overlays, and 12-column spans: [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md).\n- JSX node props and sizing mechanics: [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md).\n- Tailwind-like visual strings: [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md).\n- Inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops: [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md).\n\n## Quick start\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n});\n\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\nslide.background.fill = \"slate-50\";\n\nconst headline = slide.shapes.add({\n  geometry: \"textbox\",\n  name: \"headline\",\n  position: { left: 72, top: 64, width: 720, height: 96 },\n  fill: \"none\",\n  line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n});\nheadline.text = \"Editable headline\";\nheadline.text.style = { fontSize: 44, bold: true, color: \"slate-950\" };\n\nconst shape = slide.shapes.add({\n  geometry: \"roundRect\",\n  name: \"summary-surface\",\n  position: { left: 72, top: 188, width: 520, height: 300 },\n  fill: \"white\",\n  line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n  borderRadius: \"rounded-2xl\",\n});\n\nconst previewBlob = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 2 });\nconst layoutBlob = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\nconst montageBlob = await presentation.export({\n  format: \"webp\",\n  montage: true,\n  scale: 1,\n});\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape\",\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst help = presentation.help(\"*\", {\n  search: \"chart axis labels\",\n  include: [\"index\", \"notes\"],\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n## Load Existing Presentation Data\n\nUse `Presentation.load(proto)` when a host adapter gives the library serialized\npresentation data. The loaded object exposes the same inspect, resolve, edit,\nrender, and serialize APIs as a newly created presentation.\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = Presentation.load(proto);\n\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\",\n  search: \"Revenue\",\n  maxChars: 8000,\n});\n\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideAnchorIdFromInspect);\nconst previewBefore = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst layoutBefore = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\n\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\ntarget.text.replace(\"Revenue\", \"Revenue outlook\");\ntarget.text.style = { fontSize: 24, color: \"slate-950\", bold: true };\n\nconst previewAfter = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst layoutAfter = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\n  kind: \"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\",\n  maxChars: 3000,\n});\nconst nextProto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n## Compose-first layout\n\n```tsx\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\n\nconst presentation = Presentation.create();\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\n\nslide.compose(\n  <column width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={16}>\n    <paragraph name=\"headline\" className=\"text-slate-950 text-3xl leading-tight\">\n      <run textStyle={{ bold: true }}>Quarterly</run>\n      <run> readiness</run>\n    </paragraph>\n    <rule stroke=\"#0f172a\" width={160} weight={2} />\n  </column>,\n  {\n    frame: { left: 48, top: 40, width: 864, height: 460 },\n    baseUnit: 8,\n  },\n);\n```\n\nUse `name` for stable inspect and layout-export targeting. JSX materializing\ntags default `width` to `\"fill\"` when you omit it.\n\n## Core API Sequence\n\n- Create presentations with `Presentation.create({ slideSize })` to control default slide dimensions.\n- Add slides with `presentation.slides.add({ layout, layoutId })` or `presentation.slides.insert({ after, ... })`.\n- Use `slide.compose(nodeOrJsx, { frame, baseUnit })` for compose-first layouts. JSX lowers into the same compose runtime as the helper-based API.\n- Author content with config-first calls: `slide.shapes.add({ geometry, position, fill, line })`, `slide.images.add({ ... })`, `slide.tables.add({ ... })`, and `slide.charts.add(chartType, { ... })`.\n- Format whole-shape text with grouped configs such as `shape.text.style = { fontSize, bold, color, alignment }`.\n- Edit imported decks with `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })`, `presentation.resolve(anchorId)`, and focused facade edits.\n- Export previews with `presentation.export({ slide, format, scale })`.\n- Export deck montages with `presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 })`.\n- Export layout JSON with `slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })`.\n- Search API help with `presentation.help(query, { search, include, maxChars })`.\n- Run high-level edits with `presentation.scripts.run(kind, options)`; see [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) for the script surface.\n\n## Output Map\n\n| Output | API | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slide PNG | `presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale })` | One preview image for one slide |\n| Deck montage | `presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale })` | One overview image containing the deck slides |\n| Layout JSON | `slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })` | Structural JSON with bounds, ids, text, names, and object metadata |\n| Searchable snapshot | `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })` | NDJSON records for locating and resolving objects |\n| Runtime handoff | `presentation.toProto()` | Serializable presentation data for host adapters |\n\n## Minimal Patterns\n\nUse these as the first API patterns to reach for:\n\n```ts\n// Create, preview, inspect, then serialize.\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n});\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\nconst preview = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst montage = await presentation.export({\n  format: \"webp\",\n  montage: true,\n  scale: 1,\n});\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,chart,table\",\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n```tsx\n// Compose structure with first-principles rows/columns.\nslide.compose(\n  <row width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28}>\n    <column width={420} height=\"fill\" gap={16}>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\">\n        Title\n      </paragraph>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\">\n        Editable copy in a fixed text column.\n      </paragraph>\n    </column>\n    <box\n      width=\"fill\"\n      height=\"fill\"\n      className=\"bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl shadow-sm\"\n    />\n  </row>,\n  { frame: { left: 56, top: 56, width: 1168, height: 608 }, baseUnit: 8 },\n);\n```\n\nFor 3-column and 12-column layouts, use [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md); keep spans local with `{ mode: \"fr\", value: 1 }` track objects.\n\nUse `className` only for visual/text tokens such as `bg-*`, `rounded-*`,\n`shadow-*`, `text-*`, `font-*`, and `leading-*`. Use layout props for\n`width`, `height`, `gap`, `padding`, `align`, and `justify`.\n\n## Reference Map\n\nOpen these references as needed:\n\n- [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md) — compact JSX node surface and layout mechanics.\n- [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md) — Tailwind-like token reference for colors, text, radius, shadows, and `className`.\n- [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md) — first-principles layout recipes for rows, columns, 12-column grids, alignment, masks, and overlays.\n- [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md) — safe inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops for existing decks.\n- [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) — `Presentation` facade, slide collection, export/toProto, scripts.\n- [`references/slide.spec.md`](./references/slide.spec.md) — `Slide` API, backgrounds, placeholders, notes, export, auto-layout.\n- [`references/inspect.md`](./references/inspect.md) — grep-first snapshot (`inspect → rg → resolve/edit → re-inspect`) for loaded presentation data and templates.\n- [`references/help.md`](./references/help.md) — grep-first API and template lookup (`help → build/edit → inspect`) for presentation JS workflows.\n- [`references/layout.spec.md`](./references/layout.spec.md) — layouts, placeholders, and slide layout assignment.\n- [`references/master.spec.md`](./references/master.spec.md) — masters, layout linking, background refs, color maps.\n- [`references/theme.spec.md`](./references/theme.spec.md) — theme color schemes and hex maps.\n- [`references/styles.spec.md`](./references/styles.spec.md) — named text styles and flow through text.\n- [`references/rich-text.spec.md`](./references/rich-text.spec.md) — text blocks, ranges, links, list presets.\n- [`references/shapes.spec.md`](./references/shapes.spec.md) — shape geometry, fills, strokes, rounded corners, shadows, and z-ordering.\n- [`references/connectors.md`](./references/connectors.md) — connected lines, arrows, side anchors, direct connection sites, and rerouting behavior.\n- [`references/fill.spec.md`](./references/fill.spec.md) — fill/stroke config shapes and color shorthands, solid, gradient, pattern.\n- [`references/images.spec.md`](./references/images.spec.md) — images, cropping, contain/cover framing, prompt placeholders.\n- [`references/tables.spec.md`](./references/tables.spec.md) — tables, merges, and cell text.\n- [`references/charts.spec.md`](./references/charts.spec.md) — charts, series, axes, legends, mini-chart YAML.\n- [`references/comments.md`](./references/comments.md) — comment authors, threads, replies, reactions, and resolving imported review threads.\n- [`references/auto-layout.spec.md`](./references/auto-layout.spec.md) — deterministic layout helpers for arranging shapes within frames.\n- [`references/speaker-notes.spec.md`](./references/speaker-notes.spec.md) — speaker notes surface and visibility toggles.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3667},"formatted_output":"# Presentation Quick Start (TypeScript)\n\n## API Docs\n\nAPI docs: `api/API_DOCS.md`\n\n`Presentation` is the in-memory API object. A deck is the exported presentation\nfile. A slide is one page in the deck.\n\n## Imports\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { FileBlob, Presentation, PresentationFile } from \"@oai/artifact-tool\";\n```\n\n## Create, Render, Export\n\nThis script creates an editable deck, renders each slide PNG, writes each slide\nlayout JSON, writes a deck montage with `montage: true`, and exports PPTX.\n\n```ts\nimport fs from \"node:fs/promises\";\nimport { Presentation, PresentationFile } from \"@oai/artifact-tool\";\n\nasync function writeBlob(path: string, blob: Blob): Promise<void> {\n  await fs.writeFile(path, new Uint8Array(await blob.arrayBuffer()));\n}\n\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\n  await fs.mkdir(\"output\", { recursive: true });\n\n  const presentation = Presentation.create({\n    slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n  });\n\n  const slide = presentation.slides.add();\n  slide.background.fill = \"slate-50\";\n\n  const page = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\n  const gutter = 28;\n  const leftCol = 430;\n  const rightCol = page.width - leftCol - gutter;\n\n  const eyebrow = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: { left: page.left, top: page.top, width: 280, height: 28 },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  eyebrow.text = \"EDITABLE PRESENTATION\";\n  eyebrow.text.style = { fontSize: 12, bold: true, color: \"slate-500\" };\n\n  const title = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left,\n      top: page.top + 92,\n      width: leftCol,\n      height: 184,\n    },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  title.text = \"Build decks with editable objects\";\n  title.text.style = { fontSize: 42, bold: true, color: \"slate-950\" };\n\n  const subtitle = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"textbox\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left,\n      top: page.top + 292,\n      width: leftCol,\n      height: 96,\n    },\n    fill: \"none\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n  });\n  subtitle.text =\n    \"Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain editable.\";\n  subtitle.text.style = { fontSize: 20, color: \"slate-600\" };\n\n  const chartFrame = slide.shapes.add({\n    geometry: \"roundRect\",\n    name: \"chart-frame\",\n    position: {\n      left: page.left + leftCol + gutter,\n      top: page.top + 92,\n      width: rightCol,\n      height: 388,\n    },\n    fill: \"white\",\n    line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n    borderRadius: \"rounded-2xl\",\n    shadow: \"shadow-sm\",\n  });\n\n  slide.charts.add(\"bar\", {\n    position: {\n      left: chartFrame.position.left + 36,\n      top: chartFrame.position.top + 52,\n      width: chartFrame.position.width - 72,\n      height: 280,\n    },\n    categories: [\"Rows\", \"Grid\", \"Tokens\"],\n    series: [{ name: \"Coverage\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \"accent1\" }],\n    hasLegend: false,\n    dataLabels: { showValue: true, position: \"outEnd\" },\n    yAxis: {\n      majorGridlines: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n    },\n  });\n\n  for (const [index, slide] of presentation.slides.items.entries()) {\n    const stem = `slide-${String(index + 1).padStart(2, \"0\")}`;\n    const png = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\n    await writeBlob(`output/${stem}.png`, png);\n\n    const layout = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\n    await fs.writeFile(`output/${stem}.layout.json`, await layout.text());\n  }\n\n  const montage = await presentation.export({\n    format: \"webp\",\n    montage: true,\n    scale: 1,\n  });\n  await writeBlob(\"output/deck-montage.webp\", montage);\n\n  const pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\n  await pptx.save(\"output/deck.pptx\");\n}\n\nmain().catch((error) => {\n  console.error(error);\n  process.exitCode = 1;\n});\n```\n\n## JSX Compose Equivalent\n\nUse JSX when the slide is naturally rows, columns, grids, or overlays.\n\n```tsx\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\n/** @jsxImportSource @oai/artifact-tool/presentation-jsx */\n\nconst frame = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\n\nslide.compose(\n  <column name=\"content-frame\" width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28}>\n    <row width=\"fill\" height={72} align=\"center\" justify=\"between\">\n      <paragraph name=\"eyebrow\" className=\"text-slate-500 text-sm font-bold\">\n        EDITABLE PRESENTATION\n      </paragraph>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-400 text-sm\">Q2 planning</paragraph>\n    </row>\n    <row width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28} align=\"stretch\">\n      <column width={430} height=\"fill\" gap={18}>\n        <paragraph\n          name=\"primary-heading\"\n          className=\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\"\n        >\n          Build decks with editable objects\n        </paragraph>\n        <paragraph className=\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\">\n          Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain\n          editable.\n        </paragraph>\n      </column>\n      <box\n        name=\"chart-frame\"\n        width=\"fill\"\n        height=\"fill\"\n        className=\"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm\"\n        line={{ style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 }}\n      >\n        <chart\n          name=\"coverage-chart\"\n          chartType=\"bar\"\n          categories={[\"Rows\", \"Grid\", \"Tokens\"]}\n          series={[{ name: \"Coverage\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \"accent1\" }]}\n          hasLegend={false}\n          width=\"fill\"\n          height=\"fill\"\n        />\n      </box>\n    </row>\n  </column>,\n  { frame, baseUnit: 8 },\n);\n```\n\n## Import And Edit PPTX\n\nLoad a PPTX, inspect for stable ids, render before/after evidence, make a\nfocused edit, re-inspect, and export the edited PPTX.\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = await PresentationFile.importPptx(\n  await FileBlob.load(\"input.pptx\"),\n);\n\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\",\n  search: \"Revenue\",\n  maxChars: 8000,\n});\nconsole.log(before.ndjson);\n\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideIdFromInspect);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/before-slide.png\",\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 }),\n);\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  \"output/before-slide.layout.json\",\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })).text(),\n);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/before-montage.webp\",\n  await presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\n);\n\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\ntarget.text.replace(\"Revenue\", \"Updated revenue outlook\");\n\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/after-slide.png\",\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 }),\n);\nawait fs.writeFile(\n  \"output/after-slide.layout.json\",\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })).text(),\n);\nawait writeBlob(\n  \"output/after-montage.webp\",\n  await presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\n);\n\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\n  kind: \"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\",\n  maxChars: 3000,\n});\nconsole.log(after.ndjson);\n\nconst pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\nawait pptx.save(\"output/edited-deck.pptx\");\n```\n\n## Local Image Bytes\n\nUse byte-backed images for embedded PPTX assets.\n\n```ts\nasync function readImageBlob(imagePath: string): Promise<ArrayBuffer> {\n  const bytes = await fs.readFile(imagePath);\n  return bytes.buffer.slice(\n    bytes.byteOffset,\n    bytes.byteOffset + bytes.byteLength,\n  );\n}\n\nconst imageBytes = await readImageBlob(\"assets/product.png\");\nslide.images.add({\n  blob: imageBytes,\n  contentType: \"image/png\",\n  alt: \"Product screenshot\",\n  fit: \"cover\",\n  position: { left: 720, top: 96, width: 420, height: 280 },\n  geometry: \"roundRect\",\n  borderRadius: \"rounded-xl\",\n});\n```\n# Presentation API Docs\n\nUse the presentation facades to create PowerPoint-style decks in TypeScript.\n\n## Conventions (units + presets)\n\n- **Pixels everywhere**: all slide geometry uses CSS pixels (`px`) at 96 DPI: `position.{left,top,width,height}`, line widths, and text `fontSize`.\n- **Default canvas for examples**: use `1280 x 720` unless the task or source deck says otherwise. A useful full-slide content frame is `{ left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 }`.\n- **Angles**: rotations use degrees.\n- **Preset geometry**: `geometry` uses preset shape-name strings. Use standard shape presets and `geometry: \"custom\"` for bespoke paths.\n- **Gradients**: stop `offset` ranges from `0` to `100000`.\n- **Config-first authoring**: pass config objects into create/add APIs and grouped setters when the API provides them.\n- **String values**: options such as geometry, fit, alignment, chart type, line style, and connector kind are strings; reference pages list exact small unions and grep targets for huge catalogs.\n- **Inline docs types**: reference pages include illustrative `type ... = { ... }` blocks. Treat them as schema-shaped authoring guidance, not imports.\n- **Authoring surfaces**: `slide.compose(...)` covers rows, columns, grids, layers, and token strings. Config-first facade APIs cover exact positions, fixed chrome, native charts/tables/images, and imported deck edits.\n\n## Common Routes\n\n- Rows, columns, grids, overlays, and 12-column spans: [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md).\n- JSX node props and sizing mechanics: [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md).\n- Tailwind-like visual strings: [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md).\n- Inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops: [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md).\n\n## Quick start\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n});\n\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\nslide.background.fill = \"slate-50\";\n\nconst headline = slide.shapes.add({\n  geometry: \"textbox\",\n  name: \"headline\",\n  position: { left: 72, top: 64, width: 720, height: 96 },\n  fill: \"none\",\n  line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"none\", width: 0 },\n});\nheadline.text = \"Editable headline\";\nheadline.text.style = { fontSize: 44, bold: true, color: \"slate-950\" };\n\nconst shape = slide.shapes.add({\n  geometry: \"roundRect\",\n  name: \"summary-surface\",\n  position: { left: 72, top: 188, width: 520, height: 300 },\n  fill: \"white\",\n  line: { style: \"solid\", fill: \"slate-200\", width: 1 },\n  borderRadius: \"rounded-2xl\",\n});\n\nconst previewBlob = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 2 });\nconst layoutBlob = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\nconst montageBlob = await presentation.export({\n  format: \"webp\",\n  montage: true,\n  scale: 1,\n});\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape\",\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst help = presentation.help(\"*\", {\n  search: \"chart axis labels\",\n  include: [\"index\", \"notes\"],\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n## Load Existing Presentation Data\n\nUse `Presentation.load(proto)` when a host adapter gives the library serialized\npresentation data. The loaded object exposes the same inspect, resolve, edit,\nrender, and serialize APIs as a newly created presentation.\n\n```ts\nconst presentation = Presentation.load(proto);\n\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\",\n  search: \"Revenue\",\n  maxChars: 8000,\n});\n\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideAnchorIdFromInspect);\nconst previewBefore = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst layoutBefore = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\n\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\ntarget.text.replace(\"Revenue\", \"Revenue outlook\");\ntarget.text.style = { fontSize: 24, color: \"slate-950\", bold: true };\n\nconst previewAfter = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst layoutAfter = await slide.export({ format: \"layout\" });\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\n  kind: \"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\",\n  maxChars: 3000,\n});\nconst nextProto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n## Compose-first layout\n\n```tsx\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\n\nconst presentation = Presentation.create();\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\n\nslide.compose(\n  <column width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={16}>\n    <paragraph name=\"headline\" className=\"text-slate-950 text-3xl leading-tight\">\n      <run textStyle={{ bold: true }}>Quarterly</run>\n      <run> readiness</run>\n    </paragraph>\n    <rule stroke=\"#0f172a\" width={160} weight={2} />\n  </column>,\n  {\n    frame: { left: 48, top: 40, width: 864, height: 460 },\n    baseUnit: 8,\n  },\n);\n```\n\nUse `name` for stable inspect and layout-export targeting. JSX materializing\ntags default `width` to `\"fill\"` when you omit it.\n\n## Core API Sequence\n\n- Create presentations with `Presentation.create({ slideSize })` to control default slide dimensions.\n- Add slides with `presentation.slides.add({ layout, layoutId })` or `presentation.slides.insert({ after, ... })`.\n- Use `slide.compose(nodeOrJsx, { frame, baseUnit })` for compose-first layouts. JSX lowers into the same compose runtime as the helper-based API.\n- Author content with config-first calls: `slide.shapes.add({ geometry, position, fill, line })`, `slide.images.add({ ... })`, `slide.tables.add({ ... })`, and `slide.charts.add(chartType, { ... })`.\n- Format whole-shape text with grouped configs such as `shape.text.style = { fontSize, bold, color, alignment }`.\n- Edit imported decks with `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })`, `presentation.resolve(anchorId)`, and focused facade edits.\n- Export previews with `presentation.export({ slide, format, scale })`.\n- Export deck montages with `presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale: 1 })`.\n- Export layout JSON with `slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })`.\n- Search API help with `presentation.help(query, { search, include, maxChars })`.\n- Run high-level edits with `presentation.scripts.run(kind, options)`; see [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) for the script surface.\n\n## Output Map\n\n| Output | API | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Slide PNG | `presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale })` | One preview image for one slide |\n| Deck montage | `presentation.export({ format: \"webp\", montage: true, scale })` | One overview image containing the deck slides |\n| Layout JSON | `slide.export({ format: \"layout\" })` | Structural JSON with bounds, ids, text, names, and object metadata |\n| Searchable snapshot | `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })` | NDJSON records for locating and resolving objects |\n| Runtime handoff | `presentation.toProto()` | Serializable presentation data for host adapters |\n\n## Minimal Patterns\n\nUse these as the first API patterns to reach for:\n\n```ts\n// Create, preview, inspect, then serialize.\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\n});\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\nconst preview = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \"png\", scale: 1 });\nconst montage = await presentation.export({\n  format: \"webp\",\n  montage: true,\n  scale: 1,\n});\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\n  kind: \"slide,textbox,shape,image,chart,table\",\n  maxChars: 4000,\n});\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\n```\n\n```tsx\n// Compose structure with first-principles rows/columns.\nslide.compose(\n  <row width=\"fill\" height=\"fill\" gap={28}>\n    <column width={420} height=\"fill\" gap={16}>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\">\n        Title\n      </paragraph>\n      <paragraph className=\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\">\n        Editable copy in a fixed text column.\n      </paragraph>\n    </column>\n    <box\n      width=\"fill\"\n      height=\"fill\"\n      className=\"bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl shadow-sm\"\n    />\n  </row>,\n  { frame: { left: 56, top: 56, width: 1168, height: 608 }, baseUnit: 8 },\n);\n```\n\nFor 3-column and 12-column layouts, use [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md); keep spans local with `{ mode: \"fr\", value: 1 }` track objects.\n\nUse `className` only for visual/text tokens such as `bg-*`, `rounded-*`,\n`shadow-*`, `text-*`, `font-*`, and `leading-*`. Use layout props for\n`width`, `height`, `gap`, `padding`, `align`, and `justify`.\n\n## Reference Map\n\nOpen these references as needed:\n\n- [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md) — compact JSX node surface and layout mechanics.\n- [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md) — Tailwind-like token reference for colors, text, radius, shadows, and `className`.\n- [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md) — first-principles layout recipes for rows, columns, 12-column grids, alignment, masks, and overlays.\n- [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md) — safe inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops for existing decks.\n- [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) — `Presentation` facade, slide collection, export/toProto, scripts.\n- [`references/slide.spec.md`](./references/slide.spec.md) — `Slide` API, backgrounds, placeholders, notes, export, auto-layout.\n- [`references/inspect.md`](./references/inspect.md) — grep-first snapshot (`inspect → rg → resolve/edit → re-inspect`) for loaded presentation data and templates.\n- [`references/help.md`](./references/help.md) — grep-first API and template lookup (`help → build/edit → inspect`) for presentation JS workflows.\n- [`references/layout.spec.md`](./references/layout.spec.md) — layouts, placeholders, and slide layout assignment.\n- [`references/master.spec.md`](./references/master.spec.md) — masters, layout linking, background refs, color maps.\n- [`references/theme.spec.md`](./references/theme.spec.md) — theme color schemes and hex maps.\n- [`references/styles.spec.md`](./references/styles.spec.md) — named text styles and flow through text.\n- [`references/rich-text.spec.md`](./references/rich-text.spec.md) — text blocks, ranges, links, list presets.\n- [`references/shapes.spec.md`](./references/shapes.spec.md) — shape geometry, fills, strokes, rounded corners, shadows, and z-ordering.\n- [`references/connectors.md`](./references/connectors.md) — connected lines, arrows, side anchors, direct connection sites, and rerouting behavior.\n- [`references/fill.spec.md`](./references/fill.spec.md) — fill/stroke config shapes and color shorthands, solid, gradient, pattern.\n- [`references/images.spec.md`](./references/images.spec.md) — images, cropping, contain/cover framing, prompt placeholders.\n- [`references/tables.spec.md`](./references/tables.spec.md) — tables, merges, and cell text.\n- [`references/charts.spec.md`](./references/charts.spec.md) — charts, series, axes, legends, mini-chart YAML.\n- [`references/comments.md`](./references/comments.md) — comment authors, threads, replies, reactions, and resolving imported review threads.\n- [`references/auto-layout.spec.md`](./references/auto-layout.spec.md) — deterministic layout helpers for arranging shapes within frames.\n- [`references/speaker-notes.spec.md`](./references/speaker-notes.spec.md) — speaker notes surface and visibility toggles.\n"},"started_at_ms":1789292257692,"completed_at_ms":1789292257692}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-13T09:37:37.816Z","ordinal":4472,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a09a21-2218-7991-8273-4bf48fa68ff7","call_id":"call_xtrvJuULFXS3BmC5Lwe23NjI","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"08ec32\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":4852,\"output\":\"# Presentation Quick Start (TypeScript)\\n\\n## API Docs\\n\\nAPI docs: `api/API_DOCS.md`\\n\\n`Presentation` is the in-memory API object. A deck is the exported presentation\\nfile. A slide is one page in the deck.\\n\\n## Imports\\n\\n```ts\\nimport fs from \\\"node:fs/promises\\\";\\nimport { FileBlob, Presentation, PresentationFile } from \\\"@oai/artifact-tool\\\";\\n```\\n\\n## Create, Render, Export\\n\\nThis script creates an editable deck, renders each slide PNG, writes each slide\\nlayout JSON, writes a deck montage with `montage: true`, and exports PPTX.\\n\\n```ts\\nimport fs from \\\"node:fs/promises\\\";\\nimport { Presentation, PresentationFile } from \\\"@oai/artifact-tool\\\";\\n\\nasync function writeBlob(path: string, blob: Blob): Promise<void> {\\n  await fs.writeFile(path, new Uint8Array(await blob.arrayBuffer()));\\n}\\n\\nasync function main(): Promise<void> {\\n  await fs.mkdir(\\\"output\\\", { recursive: true });\\n\\n  const presentation = Presentation.create({\\n    slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\\n  });\\n\\n  const slide = presentation.slides.add();\\n  slide.background.fill = \\\"slate-50\\\";\\n\\n  const page = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\\n  const gutter = 28;\\n  const leftCol = 430;\\n  const rightCol = page.width - leftCol - gutter;\\n\\n  const eyebrow = slide.shapes.add({\\n    geometry: \\\"textbox\\\",\\n    position: { left: page.left, top: page.top, width: 280, height: 28 },\\n    fill: \\\"none\\\",\\n    line: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"none\\\", width: 0 },\\n  });\\n  eyebrow.text = \\\"EDITABLE PRESENTATION\\\";\\n  eyebrow.text.style = { fontSize: 12, bold: true, color: \\\"slate-500\\\" };\\n\\n  const title = slide.shapes.add({\\n    geometry: \\\"textbox\\\",\\n    position: {\\n      left: page.left,\\n      top: page.top + 92,\\n      width: leftCol,\\n      height: 184,\\n    },\\n    fill: \\\"none\\\",\\n    line: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"none\\\", width: 0 },\\n  });\\n  title.text = \\\"Build decks with editable objects\\\";\\n  title.text.style = { fontSize: 42, bold: true, color: \\\"slate-950\\\" };\\n\\n  const subtitle = slide.shapes.add({\\n    geometry: \\\"textbox\\\",\\n    position: {\\n      left: page.left,\\n      top: page.top + 292,\\n      width: leftCol,\\n      height: 96,\\n    },\\n    fill: \\\"none\\\",\\n    line: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"none\\\", width: 0 },\\n  });\\n  subtitle.text =\\n    \\\"Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain editable.\\\";\\n  subtitle.text.style = { fontSize: 20, color: \\\"slate-600\\\" };\\n\\n  const chartFrame = slide.shapes.add({\\n    geometry: \\\"roundRect\\\",\\n    name: \\\"chart-frame\\\",\\n    position: {\\n      left: page.left + leftCol + gutter,\\n      top: page.top + 92,\\n      width: rightCol,\\n      height: 388,\\n    },\\n    fill: \\\"white\\\",\\n    line: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"slate-200\\\", width: 1 },\\n    borderRadius: \\\"rounded-2xl\\\",\\n    shadow: \\\"shadow-sm\\\",\\n  });\\n\\n  slide.charts.add(\\\"bar\\\", {\\n    position: {\\n      left: chartFrame.position.left + 36,\\n      top: chartFrame.position.top + 52,\\n      width: chartFrame.position.width - 72,\\n      height: 280,\\n    },\\n    categories: [\\\"Rows\\\", \\\"Grid\\\", \\\"Tokens\\\"],\\n    series: [{ name: \\\"Coverage\\\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \\\"accent1\\\" }],\\n    hasLegend: false,\\n    dataLabels: { showValue: true, position: \\\"outEnd\\\" },\\n    yAxis: {\\n      majorGridlines: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"slate-200\\\", width: 1 },\\n    },\\n  });\\n\\n  for (const [index, slide] of presentation.slides.items.entries()) {\\n    const stem = `slide-${String(index + 1).padStart(2, \\\"0\\\")}`;\\n    const png = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 1 });\\n    await writeBlob(`output/${stem}.png`, png);\\n\\n    const layout = await slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" });\\n    await fs.writeFile(`output/${stem}.layout.json`, await layout.text());\\n  }\\n\\n  const montage = await presentation.export({\\n    format: \\\"webp\\\",\\n    montage: true,\\n    scale: 1,\\n  });\\n  await writeBlob(\\\"output/deck-montage.webp\\\", montage);\\n\\n  const pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\\n  await pptx.save(\\\"output/deck.pptx\\\");\\n}\\n\\nmain().catch((error) => {\\n  console.error(error);\\n  process.exitCode = 1;\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## JSX Compose Equivalent\\n\\nUse JSX when the slide is naturally rows, columns, grids, or overlays.\\n\\n```tsx\\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\\n/** @jsxImportSource @oai/artifact-tool/presentation-jsx */\\n\\nconst frame = { left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 };\\n\\nslide.compose(\\n  <column name=\\\"content-frame\\\" width=\\\"fill\\\" height=\\\"fill\\\" gap={28}>\\n    <row width=\\\"fill\\\" height={72} align=\\\"center\\\" justify=\\\"between\\\">\\n      <paragraph name=\\\"eyebrow\\\" className=\\\"text-slate-500 text-sm font-bold\\\">\\n        EDITABLE PRESENTATION\\n      </paragraph>\\n      <paragraph className=\\\"text-slate-400 text-sm\\\">Q2 planning</paragraph>\\n    </row>\\n    <row width=\\\"fill\\\" height=\\\"fill\\\" gap={28} align=\\\"stretch\\\">\\n      <column width={430} height=\\\"fill\\\" gap={18}>\\n        <paragraph\\n          name=\\\"primary-heading\\\"\\n          className=\\\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\\\"\\n        >\\n          Build decks with editable objects\\n        </paragraph>\\n        <paragraph className=\\\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\\\">\\n          Rows, columns, grids, charts, tables, images, and text remain\\n          editable.\\n        </paragraph>\\n      </column>\\n      <box\\n        name=\\\"chart-frame\\\"\\n        width=\\\"fill\\\"\\n        height=\\\"fill\\\"\\n        className=\\\"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm\\\"\\n        line={{ style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"slate-200\\\", width: 1 }}\\n      >\\n        <chart\\n          name=\\\"coverage-chart\\\"\\n          chartType=\\\"bar\\\"\\n          categories={[\\\"Rows\\\", \\\"Grid\\\", \\\"Tokens\\\"]}\\n          series={[{ name: \\\"Coverage\\\", values: [3, 4, 5], fill: \\\"accent1\\\" }]}\\n          hasLegend={false}\\n          width=\\\"fill\\\"\\n          height=\\\"fill\\\"\\n        />\\n      </box>\\n    </row>\\n  </column>,\\n  { frame, baseUnit: 8 },\\n);\\n```\\n\\n## Import And Edit PPTX\\n\\nLoad a PPTX, inspect for stable ids, render before/after evidence, make a\\nfocused edit, re-inspect, and export the edited PPTX.\\n\\n```ts\\nconst presentation = await PresentationFile.importPptx(\\n  await FileBlob.load(\\\"input.pptx\\\"),\\n);\\n\\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\\n  kind: \\\"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\\\",\\n  search: \\\"Revenue\\\",\\n  maxChars: 8000,\\n});\\nconsole.log(before.ndjson);\\n\\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideIdFromInspect);\\nawait writeBlob(\\n  \\\"output/before-slide.png\\\",\\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 1 }),\\n);\\nawait fs.writeFile(\\n  \\\"output/before-slide.layout.json\\\",\\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" })).text(),\\n);\\nawait writeBlob(\\n  \\\"output/before-montage.webp\\\",\\n  await presentation.export({ format: \\\"webp\\\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\\n);\\n\\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\\ntarget.text.replace(\\\"Revenue\\\", \\\"Updated revenue outlook\\\");\\n\\nawait writeBlob(\\n  \\\"output/after-slide.png\\\",\\n  await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 1 }),\\n);\\nawait fs.writeFile(\\n  \\\"output/after-slide.layout.json\\\",\\n  await (await slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" })).text(),\\n);\\nawait writeBlob(\\n  \\\"output/after-montage.webp\\\",\\n  await presentation.export({ format: \\\"webp\\\", montage: true, scale: 1 }),\\n);\\n\\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\\n  kind: \\\"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\\\",\\n  maxChars: 3000,\\n});\\nconsole.log(after.ndjson);\\n\\nconst pptx = await PresentationFile.exportPptx(presentation);\\nawait pptx.save(\\\"output/edited-deck.pptx\\\");\\n```\\n\\n## Local Image Bytes\\n\\nUse byte-backed images for embedded PPTX assets.\\n\\n```ts\\nasync function readImageBlob(imagePath: string): Promise<ArrayBuffer> {\\n  const bytes = await fs.readFile(imagePath);\\n  return bytes.buffer.slice(\\n    bytes.byteOffset,\\n    bytes.byteOffset + bytes.byteLength,\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nconst imageBytes = await readImageBlob(\\\"assets/product.png\\\");\\nslide.images.add({\\n  blob: imageBytes,\\n  contentType: \\\"image/png\\\",\\n  alt: \\\"Product screenshot\\\",\\n  fit: \\\"cover\\\",\\n  position: { left: 720, top: 96, width: 420, height: 280 },\\n  geometry: \\\"roundRect\\\",\\n  borderRadius: \\\"rounded-xl\\\",\\n});\\n```\\n# Presentation API Docs\\n\\nUse the presentation facades to create PowerPoint-style decks in TypeScript.\\n\\n## Conventions (units + presets)\\n\\n- **Pixels everywhere**: all slide geometry uses CSS pixels (`px`) at 96 DPI: `position.{left,top,width,height}`, line widths, and text `fontSize`.\\n- **Default canvas for examples**: use `1280 x 720` unless the task or source deck says otherwise. A useful full-slide content frame is `{ left: 72, top: 64, width: 1136, height: 592 }`.\\n- **Angles**: rotations use degrees.\\n- **Preset geometry**: `geometry` uses preset shape-name strings. Use standard shape presets and `geometry: \\\"custom\\\"` for bespoke paths.\\n- **Gradients**: stop `offset` ranges from `0` to `100000`.\\n- **Config-first authoring**: pass config objects into create/add APIs and grouped setters when the API provides them.\\n- **String values**: options such as geometry, fit, alignment, chart type, line style, and connector kind are strings; reference pages list exact small unions and grep targets for huge catalogs.\\n- **Inline docs types**: reference pages include illustrative `type ... = { ... }` blocks. Treat them as schema-shaped authoring guidance, not imports.\\n- **Authoring surfaces**: `slide.compose(...)` covers rows, columns, grids, layers, and token strings. Config-first facade APIs cover exact positions, fixed chrome, native charts/tables/images, and imported deck edits.\\n\\n## Common Routes\\n\\n- Rows, columns, grids, overlays, and 12-column spans: [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md).\\n- JSX node props and sizing mechanics: [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md).\\n- Tailwind-like visual strings: [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md).\\n- Inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops: [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md).\\n\\n## Quick start\\n\\n```ts\\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\\n});\\n\\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\\nslide.background.fill = \\\"slate-50\\\";\\n\\nconst headline = slide.shapes.add({\\n  geometry: \\\"textbox\\\",\\n  name: \\\"headline\\\",\\n  position: { left: 72, top: 64, width: 720, height: 96 },\\n  fill: \\\"none\\\",\\n  line: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"none\\\", width: 0 },\\n});\\nheadline.text = \\\"Editable headline\\\";\\nheadline.text.style = { fontSize: 44, bold: true, color: \\\"slate-950\\\" };\\n\\nconst shape = slide.shapes.add({\\n  geometry: \\\"roundRect\\\",\\n  name: \\\"summary-surface\\\",\\n  position: { left: 72, top: 188, width: 520, height: 300 },\\n  fill: \\\"white\\\",\\n  line: { style: \\\"solid\\\", fill: \\\"slate-200\\\", width: 1 },\\n  borderRadius: \\\"rounded-2xl\\\",\\n});\\n\\nconst previewBlob = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 2 });\\nconst layoutBlob = await slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" });\\nconst montageBlob = await presentation.export({\\n  format: \\\"webp\\\",\\n  montage: true,\\n  scale: 1,\\n});\\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\\n  kind: \\\"slide,textbox,shape\\\",\\n  maxChars: 4000,\\n});\\nconst help = presentation.help(\\\"*\\\", {\\n  search: \\\"chart axis labels\\\",\\n  include: [\\\"index\\\", \\\"notes\\\"],\\n  maxChars: 4000,\\n});\\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\\n```\\n\\n## Load Existing Presentation Data\\n\\nUse `Presentation.load(proto)` when a host adapter gives the library serialized\\npresentation data. The loaded object exposes the same inspect, resolve, edit,\\nrender, and serialize APIs as a newly created presentation.\\n\\n```ts\\nconst presentation = Presentation.load(proto);\\n\\nconst before = await presentation.inspect({\\n  kind: \\\"slide,textbox,shape,image,table,chart,notes,thread,layout\\\",\\n  search: \\\"Revenue\\\",\\n  maxChars: 8000,\\n});\\n\\nconst slide = presentation.resolve(slideAnchorIdFromInspect);\\nconst previewBefore = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 1 });\\nconst layoutBefore = await slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" });\\n\\nconst target = presentation.resolve(anchorIdFromInspect);\\ntarget.text.replace(\\\"Revenue\\\", \\\"Revenue outlook\\\");\\ntarget.text.style = { fontSize: 24, color: \\\"slate-950\\\", bold: true };\\n\\nconst previewAfter = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 1 });\\nconst layoutAfter = await slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" });\\nconst after = await presentation.inspect({\\n  target: { id: anchorIdFromInspect, beforeLines: 2, afterLines: 2 },\\n  kind: \\\"textbox,shape,image,table,chart\\\",\\n  maxChars: 3000,\\n});\\nconst nextProto = presentation.toProto();\\n```\\n\\n## Compose-first layout\\n\\n```tsx\\n/** @jsxRuntime automatic */\\n\\nconst presentation = Presentation.create();\\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\\n\\nslide.compose(\\n  <column width=\\\"fill\\\" height=\\\"fill\\\" gap={16}>\\n    <paragraph name=\\\"headline\\\" className=\\\"text-slate-950 text-3xl leading-tight\\\">\\n      <run textStyle={{ bold: true }}>Quarterly</run>\\n      <run> readiness</run>\\n    </paragraph>\\n    <rule stroke=\\\"#0f172a\\\" width={160} weight={2} />\\n  </column>,\\n  {\\n    frame: { left: 48, top: 40, width: 864, height: 460 },\\n    baseUnit: 8,\\n  },\\n);\\n```\\n\\nUse `name` for stable inspect and layout-export targeting. JSX materializing\\ntags default `width` to `\\\"fill\\\"` when you omit it.\\n\\n## Core API Sequence\\n\\n- Create presentations with `Presentation.create({ slideSize })` to control default slide dimensions.\\n- Add slides with `presentation.slides.add({ layout, layoutId })` or `presentation.slides.insert({ after, ... })`.\\n- Use `slide.compose(nodeOrJsx, { frame, baseUnit })` for compose-first layouts. JSX lowers into the same compose runtime as the helper-based API.\\n- Author content with config-first calls: `slide.shapes.add({ geometry, position, fill, line })`, `slide.images.add({ ... })`, `slide.tables.add({ ... })`, and `slide.charts.add(chartType, { ... })`.\\n- Format whole-shape text with grouped configs such as `shape.text.style = { fontSize, bold, color, alignment }`.\\n- Edit imported decks with `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })`, `presentation.resolve(anchorId)`, and focused facade edits.\\n- Export previews with `presentation.export({ slide, format, scale })`.\\n- Export deck montages with `presentation.export({ format: \\\"webp\\\", montage: true, scale: 1 })`.\\n- Export layout JSON with `slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" })`.\\n- Search API help with `presentation.help(query, { search, include, maxChars })`.\\n- Run high-level edits with `presentation.scripts.run(kind, options)`; see [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) for the script surface.\\n\\n## Output Map\\n\\n| Output | API | Result |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Slide PNG | `presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale })` | One preview image for one slide |\\n| Deck montage | `presentation.export({ format: \\\"webp\\\", montage: true, scale })` | One overview image containing the deck slides |\\n| Layout JSON | `slide.export({ format: \\\"layout\\\" })` | Structural JSON with bounds, ids, text, names, and object metadata |\\n| Searchable snapshot | `presentation.inspect({ kind, search, maxChars })` | NDJSON records for locating and resolving objects |\\n| Runtime handoff | `presentation.toProto()` | Serializable presentation data for host adapters |\\n\\n## Minimal Patterns\\n\\nUse these as the first API patterns to reach for:\\n\\n```ts\\n// Create, preview, inspect, then serialize.\\nconst presentation = Presentation.create({\\n  slideSize: { width: 1280, height: 720 },\\n});\\nconst slide = presentation.slides.add();\\nconst preview = await presentation.export({ slide, format: \\\"png\\\", scale: 1 });\\nconst montage = await presentation.export({\\n  format: \\\"webp\\\",\\n  montage: true,\\n  scale: 1,\\n});\\nconst snapshot = await presentation.inspect({\\n  kind: \\\"slide,textbox,shape,image,chart,table\\\",\\n  maxChars: 4000,\\n});\\nconst proto = presentation.toProto();\\n```\\n\\n```tsx\\n// Compose structure with first-principles rows/columns.\\nslide.compose(\\n  <row width=\\\"fill\\\" height=\\\"fill\\\" gap={28}>\\n    <column width={420} height=\\\"fill\\\" gap={16}>\\n      <paragraph className=\\\"text-slate-950 text-5xl font-bold leading-tight\\\">\\n        Title\\n      </paragraph>\\n      <paragraph className=\\\"text-slate-600 text-xl leading-relaxed\\\">\\n        Editable copy in a fixed text column.\\n      </paragraph>\\n    </column>\\n    <box\\n      width=\\\"fill\\\"\\n      height=\\\"fill\\\"\\n      className=\\\"bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl shadow-sm\\\"\\n    />\\n  </row>,\\n  { frame: { left: 56, top: 56, width: 1168, height: 608 }, baseUnit: 8 },\\n);\\n```\\n\\nFor 3-column and 12-column layouts, use [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md); keep spans local with `{ mode: \\\"fr\\\", value: 1 }` track objects.\\n\\nUse `className` only for visual/text tokens such as `bg-*`, `rounded-*`,\\n`shadow-*`, `text-*`, `font-*`, and `leading-*`. Use layout props for\\n`width`, `height`, `gap`, `padding`, `align`, and `justify`.\\n\\n## Reference Map\\n\\nOpen these references as needed:\\n\\n- [`references/jsx.md`](./references/jsx.md) — compact JSX node surface and layout mechanics.\\n- [`references/tokens.md`](./references/tokens.md) — Tailwind-like token reference for colors, text, radius, shadows, and `className`.\\n- [`references/cookbook/layout.md`](./references/cookbook/layout.md) — first-principles layout recipes for rows, columns, 12-column grids, alignment, masks, and overlays.\\n- [`references/cookbook/imported-deck.md`](./references/cookbook/imported-deck.md) — safe inspect, resolve, edit, preview, and re-inspect loops for existing decks.\\n- [`references/presentation.spec.md`](./references/presentation.spec.md) — `Presentation` facade, slide collection, export/toProto, scripts.\\n- [`references/slide.spec.md`](./references/slide.spec.md) — `Slide` API, backgrounds, placeholders, notes, export, auto-layout.\\n- [`references/inspect.md`](./references/inspect.md) — grep-first snapshot (`inspect → rg → resolve/edit → re-inspect`) for loaded presentation data and templates.\\n- [`references/help.md`](./references/help.md) — grep-first API and template lookup (`help → build/edit → inspect`) for presentation JS workflows.\\n- [`references/layout.spec.md`](./references/layout.spec.md) — layouts, placeholders, and slide layout assignment.\\n- [`references/master.spec.md`](./references/master.spec.md) — masters, layout linking, background refs, color maps.\\n- [`references/theme.spec.md`](./references/theme.spec.md) — theme color schemes and hex maps.\\n- [`references/styles.spec.md`](./references/styles.spec.md) — named text styles and flow through text.\\n- [`references/rich-text.spec.md`](./references/rich-text.spec.md) — text blocks, ranges, links, list presets.\\n- [`references/shapes.spec.md`](./references/shapes.spec.md) — shape geometry, fills, strokes, rounded corners, shadows, and z-ordering.\\n- [`references/connectors.md`](./references/connectors.md) — connected lines, arrows, side anchors, direct connection sites, and rerouting behavior.\\n- [`references/fill.spec.md`](./references/fill.spec.md) — fill/stroke config shapes and color shorthands, solid, gradient, pattern.\\n- [`references/images.spec.md`](./references/images.spec.md) — images, cropping, contain/cover framing, prompt placeholders.\\n- [`references/tables.spec.md`](./references/tables.spec.md) — tables, merges, and cell text.\\n- [`references/charts.spec.md`](./references/charts.spec.md) — charts, series, axes, legends, mini-chart YAML.\\n- [`references/comments.md`](./references/comments.md) — comment authors, threads, replies, reactions, and resolving imported review threads.\\n- [`references/auto-layout.spec.md`](./references/auto-layout.spec.md) — deterministic layout helpers for arranging shapes within frames.\\n- [`references/speaker-notes.spec.md`](./references/speaker-notes.spec.md) — speaker notes surface and visibility toggles.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"9ee778\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000001167,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":30,\"output\":\"/var/folders/j4/4j7qn2vd4zd6ykklypxn1d540000gn/T/perigee-results.9Xj5K0Y1zD/tmp/template-inspect/template-manifest.json\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a09a1f-5842-7af1-ac12-7cf624fbc8c9","create_time":1789292257.816149}}}
